    "knowledge_point": "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function",
    "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cot⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The function has no minimum value. $$\n- $x=-4\\pi $ is in the domain of the function. $$\n- $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function.",
    "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934292/assets/8bc549c68a3bc5b7989ac1835e4bb58183066c7797264b8cccd4f3fd2c895056.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function has no minimum or maximum value. $$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $n\\pi $ for any integer $n$, thus it is not defined for $x=-4\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is true. The zeros of $y=cot⁡x$ occur at $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ for any integer $n.$ Therefore, $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function.",
